  "estimatedMinutes": 25,
  "instructions": "## Branch, hub, branch\n\nA bank has a hub router **HUB** in Accra with two branches: Kumasi (`172.16.1.0/24`, router KSI) and Tamale (`172.16.3.0/24`, router TML). The hub also hosts the core banking server on `172.16.0.0/24`. The branch routers have only one way out, so a **default route** is enough for them. The hub needs a **specific route** to each branch.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Add a default route on KSI and on TML pointing at the hub.\n2. Add routes on HUB for each branch network via the right branch router.\n3. Check that Kumasi reaches the server and Tamale, then answer the question about longest-prefix match.",
